<exercisegroup cols="2" xml:id="exercisegroup-col-row-null-space-colspace">
<title>TITLE</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each of the following:
	<ol>
		<li> Determine the value of <m> k </m> so that the column space of <m> A </m> is a subspace of <m> \R^k </m>. </li>
		<li xml:id="instruction-exercisegroup-col-row-null-space-colspace-basis">
			Form a basis for the column space of <m> A </m> from the columns of <m> A </m>.
		</li>
		<li>
			Express each of the other columns of <m> A </m> as a linear combination of your basis vectors from
			<xref ref="instruction-exercisegroup-col-row-null-space-colspace-basis" text="custom">part</xref>.
		</li>
		<li> Determine the value of <m> k </m> so that the row space of <m> A </m> is a subspace of <m> \R^k </m>. </li>
		<li> Determine a basis for the row space of <m> A </m>.  </li>
		<li> Determine the value of <m> k </m> so that the null space of <m> A </m> is a subspace of <m> \R^k </m>. </li>
		<li> Determine a basis for the null space of <m> A </m>. </li>
		<li>
			State the rank and nullity of <m> A </m>,
			and confirm the <xref ref="theorem-col-row-null-space-rank-nullity" text="title" /> in this case.
		</li>
	</ol>
</p></introduction>

<exercise>
	<statement><p>
		INDIVIDUAL PROBLEM
	</p></statement>
	<answer><p>
		ANSWER (or change to a solution element)
	</p></answer>
</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
